    content: "To attribute a Stripe payment to a sales rep, match each payment to the call that produced it, then carry that call's closer, setter and lead source onto the payment. The hard part is that the checkout email often does not match the booking email, so you need a way to match by name, email or date and fix the exceptions. RevPhlo syncs payments from Stripe or any other payment processor automatically and links each one to the exact call, closer, setter and source.\n\nI spent years reconciling Stripe against the CRM by hand at the end of the month. It took hours, it was always a little wrong, and commissions depended on it. Here is a process that holds up.\n\n## Why Stripe payments are hard to credit to a rep\n\nStripe knows who paid and how much. It does not know who sold the deal. Your CRM knows who owns the opportunity. Your calendar knows who booked the call. None of them alone can tell you which rep produced the cash.\n\nCommon reasons a payment ends up unmatched:\n\n* **Different emails.** A prospect books with a personal email and pays with a work email, or a spouse pays.\n* **Payment plans.** One deal creates several charges over months.\n* **Failed charges.** The CRM says closed won, and the card declined.\n* **Refunds and chargebacks.** The original sale is reversed later, often with no link back to the deal.\n* **Reassigned deals.** A follow-up call is taken by a different closer than the first call.\n\n## A simple attribution process that works\n\n1. **Capture the source when the lead is created.** Store the original source, campaign and funnel, using GoHighLevel tags, fields or UTMs.\n2. **Record who touched the deal.** Save the setter who booked the call and the closer who took it, and keep the history if the deal is reassigned.\n3. **Log the call outcome.** Mark whether the call happened and how it ended.\n4. **Match every payment to a call.** Match automatically on email where you can, and search by name or date where you cannot.\n5. **Track the full life of the payment.** Keep initial cash, later installments, failed payments, refunds and chargebacks as separate events.\n6. **Review unmatched payments weekly.** The exceptions tell you which part of the process needs fixing.\n\n## Decide the credit rules before commissions are due\n\nWrite these down so nobody argues about them at payout:\n\n* Which system is the source of truth for collected cash\n* Whether the closer of record is the person on the first call or the deciding call\n* How setters get credit for the calls they booked\n* What happens to commission when a payment fails, refunds or charges back\n* How payment plan installments are credited over time\n\n## Mistakes that throw off rep attribution\n\n* **Paying on CRM stage instead of Stripe.** Pay commission on money that arrived in Stripe, since a CRM stage only records a commitment.\n* **Overwriting the owner field.** If a deal moves to a new closer, the old call should keep its original closer.\n* **Ignoring the setter.** Show rate and booked revenue are setter metrics, and setters deserve credit for calls that turn into cash.\n* **Doing it once a month.** By then, failed payments are cold and nobody remembers the context.\n\n## How RevPhlo handles Stripe payment attribution\n\nRevPhlo connects to your Stripe account or any other payment processor, your CRM (GoHighLevel or HubSpot), and your call recordings from Fathom.\n\n* **Payments sync automatically** from Stripe or any other payment processor.\n* **Every payment is linked to the call.** RevPhlo links a Stripe payment to the exact call, closer, setter and source.\n* **Mismatched emails are handled.** When the paying email does not match the appointment email, search by name, email or date, match it to the right call, and the attribution data syncs.\n* **Failed-charge alerts.** When a charge fails, RevPhlo sends an alert so someone can follow up while the deal is still warm.\n* **Refunds adjust closer revenue.** When a payment is refunded, the closer's revenue is adjusted, so commissions and rankings reflect what was actually kept.\n* **Reassignment history.** When a payment is reassigned to a different rep, RevPhlo keeps the history, so you can see who held the credit before.\n* **Commission tracking with custom splits.**\n* **Revenue by closer, source and funnel**, so you can see if your top rep is converting or just getting the warmest calls.\n* **Leaderboards and rep portals** show cash collected, so rankings reflect money that actually arrived.\n\nFor more on the gap between CRM numbers and Stripe, read [Stripe payment matching for sales teams](https://www.revphlo.com/blog/stripe-payment-matching-sales-teams). For the reporting side, see [how to track revenue by closer](https://www.revphlo.com/blog/how-to-track-revenue-by-closer).\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### How do I know which sales rep made a Stripe sale?\n\nMatch the payment to the call that produced it, then carry that call's closer, setter and lead source onto the payment. Match on email first, and search by name or date when the emails differ.\n\n### Why don't my Stripe payments match my CRM?\n\nA CRM stage only records a commitment. Failed charges, payment plans, refunds and chargebacks all create gaps between what the CRM shows as closed and what Stripe shows as collected.\n\n### Should commission be paid on CRM deals or Stripe payments?\n\nOn collected payments. Write clear rules for failed payments, refunds, chargebacks and payment plan installments before the first payout.\n\n### Does RevPhlo work with payment processors other than Stripe?\n\nYes. RevPhlo works with Stripe and any other payment processor.\n\n### What happens in RevPhlo when a payment fails or is refunded?\n\nRevPhlo sends failed-charge alerts, and refunds adjust the closer's revenue, so attribution and commissions stay accurate.\n\n### Can RevPhlo handle split commissions?\n\nYes. RevPhlo lists commission tracking with custom splits as part of payment matching.\n\n## Find the payments you cannot attribute today\n\nBring your current GoHighLevel and Stripe setup. In a 20-minute diagnostic, we will map your post-booking pipeline and show you where leads and attribution are falling through the cracks.\n\n**[Find your team's data leaks](https://www.revphlo.com/#book)**",
