    content: "A sales leaderboard for closers should rank reps by cash collected, then show close rate, show rate and revenue per call next to each name. It needs to update from your real systems, your CRM and Stripe, so reps trust it and nobody spends an hour a day fixing a spreadsheet. RevPhlo provides live leaderboards ranked by cash collected, close rate, show rate and revenue per call, updated as payments process.\n\nEvery high-ticket team I have worked with had some version of a leaderboard. Most were a Google Sheet that someone updated at night, with duplicate ranks and a note to recount. Here is how to build one closers will actually pay attention to.\n\n## Rank by outcomes, not activity\n\nActivity boards rank calls made, dials or demos booked. They are easy to measure, and reps learn to game them fast. They book unqualified calls, rush discovery and keep calls short to hit volume.\n\nFor closers, rank by outcomes:\n\n* **Cash collected.** Money that actually reached Stripe or your payment processor, matched to the closer who made the sale. It is the hardest number to game because a real customer has to pay.\n* **Close rate.** Payments divided by calls taken, meaning calls where the prospect showed up. A closer with a high rate on fewer calls may be more valuable than one with a low rate on many.\n* **Show rate.** The share of booked calls that actually happen, with a clear rule for reschedules, cancellations and no-shows. This matters most for setters, and it explains why one closer had fewer chances than another.\n* **Revenue per call.** Cash collected divided by calls taken. It combines close rate and deal size in one number.\n* **Average deal value.** Shows whether a rep sells the full offer or defaults to the smallest package.\n\n## Why it needs to be live\n\nWhen a closer takes a payment and sees their name move up the board within minutes, the win registers while it still matters to them.\n\nA live board also helps managers. If it is Wednesday and a closer has no closes, you can coach today instead of finding out in the weekly report.\n\nLive data has one requirement. The numbers have to come straight from your CRM, payment processor and call recordings. End of day reports and spreadsheet exports cannot keep up.\n\n## How to set up a closer leaderboard\n\n1. **Pick one primary ranking.** Cash collected for the current period works for most high-ticket teams.\n2. **Add context columns.** Close rate, show rate, revenue per call and average deal value.\n3. **Define every metric in writing.** What counts as a call taken, a close and collected cash. Decide how refunds and failed payments are handled.\n4. **Connect the data sources.** Calls and appointments from the CRM, payments from Stripe, outcomes from call recordings.\n5. **Give setters their own view.** Calls booked, show rate on those bookings and the revenue those bookings produced.\n6. **Pair the board with private rep stats.** Some reps improve faster when they can also see their own trends privately, away from the public board.\n\n## Mistakes that make leaderboards backfire\n\n* **Ranking on CRM \"closed won.\"** Deals marked closed that never paid will inflate the board and erode trust in it.\n* **Ignoring lead quality.** A closer who gets warmer leads will look better. Show revenue by source next to the board when you review it.\n* **Using it to shame people.** The same data that ranks a struggling rep should start a coaching conversation, such as looking at why their show rate dropped.\n* **Letting it go stale.** A board that is wrong once loses the room.\n\nOur post on [sales leaderboards beyond vanity metrics](https://www.revphlo.com/blog/sales-leaderboards-beyond-vanity-metrics) covers the culture side in more depth.\n\n## How RevPhlo builds the leaderboard for you\n\nRevPhlo connects to GoHighLevel or HubSpot, Stripe or any other payment processor, and Fathom, so the leaderboard fills itself.\n\n* **Live leaderboards** ranked by cash collected, close rate, show rate and revenue per call, updated in real time as payments process.\n* **Setter view.** Setters get their own leaderboard view.\n* **Trends and time filters.** See how each rep is moving over time and filter the board by time period.\n* **Rep drill-downs.** Click into any rep to see the numbers behind their rank.\n* **Payments matched to the right closer.** Payments sync automatically and link to the call, closer, setter and source.\n* **Refunds adjust closer revenue**, so the board reflects money the closer actually kept.\n* **Failed-charge alerts**, so someone follows up on a declined card.\n* **Close rate is payments divided by calls taken**, and show rate is blended to account for reschedules, cancellations and no-shows.\n* **Rep portals.** Every rep gets a portal with personal KPIs, a daily task queue, call recordings and shareable leaderboard wins to Slack or Instagram.\n* **Revenue by closer, source and funnel**, so you can see if your top rep is converting or just getting the warmest calls.\n\nGoHighLevel does not have a built-in leaderboard, which is why so many GHL teams use a sheet. See [RevPhlo vs GoHighLevel reporting](https://www.revphlo.com/compare/revphlo-vs-gohighlevel-reporting) for the full comparison, or try the [interactive demo](https://www.revphlo.com/demo) with sample data.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### What should a sales leaderboard for closers track?\n\nRank by cash collected, then show close rate, show rate, revenue per call and average deal value. Avoid ranking closers on activity like dials or calls made.\n\n### How does RevPhlo handle refunds on the leaderboard?\n\nRefunds adjust the closer's revenue, so the leaderboard reflects cash the closer actually kept. RevPhlo also sends failed-charge alerts.\n\n### How often should a sales leaderboard update?\n\nAs close to real time as you can. A board that moves when payments land keeps the win fresh and lets managers coach the same week.\n\n### Should setters be on the same leaderboard as closers?\n\nGive setters their own view based on calls booked, show rate and the revenue their bookings produced. Their job and their numbers are different. RevPhlo includes a setter view of the leaderboard.\n\n### Does GoHighLevel have a sales leaderboard?\n\nGoHighLevel does not have a built-in leaderboard feature, so most GHL teams build one in Google Sheets. RevPhlo adds live leaderboards on top of GoHighLevel and Stripe data.\n\n## Put a live leaderboard in front of your closers\n\nBring your current GoHighLevel and Stripe setup. In a 20-minute diagnostic, we will map your post-booking pipeline and show you where leads and attribution are falling through the cracks.\n\n**[Find your team's data leaks](https://www.revphlo.com/#book)**",
